<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hajji Chelebi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1755">1755</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Haji Chalabi Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hajji Chelebi was a notable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaki-azerbaijan">Shaki</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> who in 1743 led a rising against the heavy taxes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> and defeated the forces sent against him. He made Shaki an independent khanate, the first of the Caucasian khanates to break from Persian rule, and campaigned against neighbouring powers until his death.</p></div>
